WHY THIS EXISTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Application stores — Apple's App Store, Google Play, and others — require
distributors to accept terms that place restrictions on end users beyond those in
the AGPL. Section 6 of the AGPL forbids imposing further restrictions on the
rights it grants, which makes distribution through such stores legally uncertain.

Without an explicit exception, anyone who forks this project cannot ship their
fork through an application store — even though we can, as the copyright holder.
That is not the outcome we want. This permission removes the obstacle for
everyone.


